# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/dashboard-power (mode 0440).
#
# Lets the dashboard UI trigger a clean shutdown from the config modal, so the
# board can be unplugged without risking SD-card corruption from a write in
# flight. There is no keyboard on a wall-mounted display and no one is going to
# SSH in before switching it off at the socket.
#
# Kept in a separate file from dashboard-update.sudoers on purpose: that one
# exists for the unattended updater, this one is reachable from the touchscreen,
# and the two shouldn't widen each other.
#
# Scoped to poweroff alone -- deliberately NOT reboot, NOT halt, NOT blanket
# NOPASSWD.
#
# CAVEAT, so nobody mistakes this for a security control it isn't: stock
# Raspberry Pi OS installs /etc/sudoers.d/010_pi-nopasswd containing
#     pi ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
# which already grants `pi` unrestricted passwordless root. While that file is
# present this rule grants nothing new, and the same is true of
# dashboard-update.sudoers. Its value is that the app's required privilege is
# declared explicitly, so the board still works if you later delete the blanket
# rule -- which is the thing actually worth doing if you want this locked down.
pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl poweroff, /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff
